                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Your standard VN in anime episodic format with lots of dialogues. It's a Kinetic VN with no decision making. It is based on the characters from teh \"Fruit of Grisaia\" but follows a different story. I haven't the second part and I'm not sure if I will. Probably I might do it to complete the series but not for any other reason.\r\n\r\nI started playing VNs a long time back and playing this brought me to the initial days where I would not skip scenes nor dialogues. But now, I was rushing to complete this. There's a lot of WTF moments and twists you can spot from far off. I did contemplate dropping it entirely but decided to power through.\r\n\r\nThere's a bit of humour, magical girl stuff, nonsensical back and forth and many more usual anime tropes. But I personally found it tedious after 20 mins into the VN.\r\n\r\nI would generally downvote this, BUT... If you're new to the VN genre and anime, there's a tiny chance this will stay with you. It could also make you decide not to play VNs after this. Either ways, this barely makes the cut - however I won't recommend this to anyone. \r\n\r\nNo. Seriously - there's a lot of awesome anime where these tropes are dealt better. Go watch them.",
